{
  "about": "Requests that each carry one value under a name, grouped by what each group shows. A row sends method to target with value under name in its query, its form, its JSON body (a string, or a list of one string for json-list) or a header (at); on says whether the value is public there: its name is one the public-name table lists (packages/contracts/src/public-request-names.ts, and Go's public_names_generated.go from it), on a route its contract names or on any route where it names none. Every other value is a credential like any other. Go's public_routes_test.go reads every row through an answer that quotes the value (ReadAnswer, then Words), which prints it where it is public and redacts it elsewhere, and public-request-routes.test.ts through requestCredentials, which leaves it out where it is public and holds it elsewhere. Every value here is made up.",
